<section class="r-section soft" id="faq">
<div class="r-wrap"><span class="r-kicker">PRACTICAL ANSWERS</span>
<h2>Real estate marketing questions, answered.</h2>
<div class="r-faqs">
<details><summary>How can real estate agents generate more leads?</summary><p>Start with a defined market and client type, then combine intent-based advertising, relevant landing pages and prompt CRM follow-up. Buyer and seller inquiries should follow different qualification and appointment workflows.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you generate buyer leads or seller leads?</summary><p>Both. Buyer campaigns can focus on home searches and property interests. Seller campaigns can focus on listing consultations and local market information. Each requires different messaging, qualification and follow-up.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Google Ads work for real estate agents?</summary><p>Google Ads can capture active demand when targeting, budgets and landing pages align with a specific market. Measure qualified conversations rather than clicks alone.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can you advertise listings on Facebook and Instagram?</summary><p>Yes, where the advertiser has the required rights and permissions. Housing campaigns must comply with Meta&#x27;s Special Ad Category rules and applicable fair housing laws.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will you connect leads to our existing CRM?</summary><p>We assess the brokerage&#x27;s current CRM and lead-routing process first, then plan supported integrations, follow-up ownership and appointment workflows.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee listings or closed deals?</summary><p>No. Marketing can improve how relevant inquiries are attracted and handled, but appointments, listings and transactions depend on multiple factors outside advertising.</p></details>
</div>
</div>
